WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Start a research investigation without knowing a prior or posterior. Define the event, collect research, choose starting assumptions, and let the app calculate the updated result.

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:24.000
In the explorer, choose New investigation. Name it Radish germination. A new workspace starts without papers or observations.

3
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Write: At least 60% of radish seeds germinate within seven days under controlled conditions. In guided analysis setup, define the event as a visible radicle by day seven. No observations yet? Choose Not yet and continue reviewing papers.

4
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Open literature, then Add a link. Paste the example DOI, inspect its metadata, and follow the original source. Its conditions differ from our teaching scenario.

5
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Open evidence.json. Read the verbatim excerpt and the original source. Mark its relationship Inconclusive for this scenario; classification does not update the model.

6
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:32.000
In analysis.py, define the event, choose I have event counts, and select Little previous knowledge. Enter 34 events in 50 observations and mark them synthetic. The app calculates a 67.3% updated estimate; you do not enter a posterior.

7
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:46.000
In research-notes.md, record the event definition, sampling design, independence assumptions, and limitations. The interval crosses 60%; the mean alone does not confirm the hypothesis.

8
00:01:46.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Save with the toolbar or Ctrl/Cmd S. Open report.md and export Markdown or JSON. Keep sources, observations, priors, annotations, and notes together for reproducibility.
